  <datafield tag="590" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Box of Library's c.1 addressed in red ink to: George Wittenborn Inc., 1018 Madison Avenue, New York NY 10021 USA. It is stamped on the bottom in black ink: Diter Rot, Little tentative recipe, Edition HJ Mayer. It bears 3 British postage stamps cancelled: Hampstead S.D.O. 20 OCT 69 10 AM.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="590" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Box of Library's c.2 addressed in black ink to: Miss J. Reichart, 12 Belsize Park Gardens, London, N.W.3. It is stamped on the bottom and top in black ink: Diter Rot, Little tentative recipe, Watford School of Art. It bears 1 British postage stamp cancelled: Watford 2 JUNE 69.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Produced between January 1968 and March 1969 at Watford School of Art, England. Printed through a Rotaprint R70 in an edition of 100. 1 to 50, Edition Hansjorg Mayer. 50 to 100, Watford School of Art"--Leaf [2].</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Little tentative recipe: PRINT until you cant stand it anymore or [until] you dont want anymore, take away, for binding for instance, the sheets which the machine cannot take anymore (torn, wrinkled, or beautiful according to someone's taste), dont throw anything away"--Leaf [3].</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Issued in wooden box 10 x 10 x 11 cm.</subfield>
  </datafield>
